used": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {"implementer": 1}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 2, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "`/api/decks` now leaves out decks that have no match picked to them, and each deck carries `first_played`, its earliest match start. The version date range in the frontend starts from `first_played` and falls back to `first_seen` only when there is none.\n\nI re-ran the listed checks myself after the implementer finished, and all of them pass:\n- **`tests/test_api.py`:** 183 passed.\n- **`ruff`:** clean.\n- **`tsc -b`:** exit 0.\n- **`pnpm --dir web lint`:** passed.\n- **`pnpm --dir web test`:** I only saw the tail of the output. It showed no failures. The implementer reported 496 passed.\n- **`gen:types`:** I didn't re-run it. The implementer ran it, and `web/src/types/api.ts` is among the modified files.\n\nThe changes are in `common.py` (the new `Deck` field), `meta.py` (one query with a grouped CTE and `WHERE s.matches_played > 0`), `deckOverview.ts` and the regenerated `api.ts`. I read the diff for the first three and it matches the spec. I didn't open `api.ts`, as the project instructions say, and I didn't check the dashboard against a real database.", "ttft_ms": 1463, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 32271, "uuid": "fab20e69-eefe-4171-9b41-274ca275cc89", "ttft_stream_ms": 1065, "time_to_request_ms": 15, "first_content_frame_ms": 1065, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 1}
